லேன்","parts":[{"text":"செல்","lemma":"cel","gloss":"go"},{"text":"ஏன்","lemma":"ēṉ","gloss":"first person singular negative suffix"}],"gloss":"I will not go"},{"surface":"அவன்","parts":[{"text":"அவன்","lemma":"avaṉ","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"குன்று","parts":[{"text":"குன்று","lemma":"kuṉṟu","gloss":"hill"}],"gloss":"hill"},{"surface":"கெழு","parts":[{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"keḻu","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"abounding in"},{"surface":"நாட்டே","parts":[{"text":"நாட்டே","lemma":"நாட்டே","gloss":"to the country indeed"}],"gloss":"to the country indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Bow-rubbed erect sandal-smeared of chest / sounding-water paddy-field white-umbrella lord / strength-abiding broad-hand sharp-sword Kuttuvan / generous-man being world even if praises / thinking avoid, O high-worded poets! / I too, dark-moonlight passed day-making dawn / one-eyed great-kiṇai-drum to sound clearly having beaten / sound-roaring drum's well-made chariot's father / unfading Vañci sang as / heart-overflowing with joy approaching desiring / having killed anger unappeased flesh-smelling of tusk / fierce-anger elephant he granted, having feared / I that returned as, himself that / small-thing saying realizing having felt ashamed, another also one / great male elephant granted he indeed, because of that / great large kinfolk great distress even if experiences / difficult to approach gift he will give saying / always I will not go his hill-abounding country indeed","translation":"O poets of noble words! Even if the world praises Kuttuvan—the lord of the white umbrella and fertile fields watered by roaring streams, whose broad hands possess great strength and a sharp sword, and whose chest is smeared with sandalwood paste rubbed by his bow—do not think of going to him. For I too, at dawn when the dark night had passed and daylight was breaking, beat my single-headed great kiṇai drum to sound clearly, and sang of Vañci, the unfading capital of his father who possessed roaring war drums and swift chariots. Desiring to approach him with a heart full of joy, he granted me a fierce elephant with flesh-smelling tusks whose anger from killing was still unappeased. Fearing its wildness, I refused it. Realizing that he had given something too small and feeling ashamed, he then granted me another great male elephant! Therefore, even if my large family suffers great distress, I will never again go to his hill-abounding country, thinking, 'He will give me a gift that is hard to obtain.'","modern":"வில் உராய்ந்து நிமிர்ந்த, சந்தனம் பூசிய மார்பையும், ஒலிக்கும் நீர் பாயும் வயல்களையும், வெண்கொற்றக் குடையையும் உடைய தலைவனும், வலிமை பொருந்திய பெரிய கைகளையும் கூர்மையான வாளையும் உடையவனுமாகிய குட்டுவன் கொடையாளி என்று உலகமே புகழ்ந்தாலும், உயர்ந்த சொற்களைப் பேசும் புலவர்களே, அவனிடம் செல்வதை நினைக்காதீர்கள்! ஏனெனில், இருள் விலகி விடியற்காலைப் பொழுது வந்தபோது, நான் எனது ஒரு கண் கொண்ட பெரிய கிணைப் பறையை ஒலிக்கச் செய்து, முழங்கும் முரசும் தேரும் உடைய அவனது தந்தையின் வாடாத வஞ்சி நகரைப் பாடினேன். மனநிறைவோடு அவனை அணுக விரும்பிய எனக்கு, அவன் போர்க்களத்தில் கொன்று சினம் தணியாத, புலால் நாற்றமுடைய தந்தங்களை உடைய சினங்கொண்ட யானையைப் பரிசாக அளித்தான். நான் அதற்கு அஞ்சி அதனை மறுத்தேன். தான் கொடுத்தது சிறியது என்று உணர்ந்து நாணிய அவன், எனக்குப் பிறிதொரு பெரிய ஆண் யானையைப் பரிசாக அளித்தான். அதனால், எனது பெரிய சுற்றத்தார் பெரும் வறுமையால் வாடினாலும், 'அவன் பெறுதற்கரிய பரிசிலைத் தருவான்' என்று எண்ணி, அவனது குன்றுகள் நிறைந்த நாட்டிற்கு நான் இனி ஒருபோதும் செல்ல மாட்டேன்.","explanation":"This poem is addressed to other poets by the poet Kōṉāṭṭu Eṟiccalūr Māṭalaṉ Maturai Kumaṟaṉār, praising the Chera chieftain Cōḻiya Ēṉāti Tirukkuṭṭuvaṉ. The poet humorously warns other poets not to visit the chieftain, claiming that his generosity is overwhelmingly terrifying. He recounts how he sang of the king's father and the capital Vañci at dawn, and the king gifted him a fierce, battle-hardened elephant. When the poet refused it out of fear, the king felt ashamed that his gift was too \"small\" and immediately gifted him an even larger male elephant. The poet concludes that even if his family starves, he will not go back to that mountainous country because the gifts are too grand and terrifying to handle. The key words are vaḷḷiyaṉ (generous man), kiṇai (drum), vēḻam (elephant), and parisil (gift).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.4],[0.7,1.2],[1.2,1.71],[1.71,2.2],[2.2,3.2],[3.2,3.6],[3.6,3.8],[3.8,4.2],[4.2,4.2],[4.2,6.0],[6.0,6.3],[6.3,6.57],[6.57,6.57],[6.57,6.6],[6.6,8.7],[8.7,9.0],[9.0,10.1],[10.1,10.3],[10.3,10.3],[10.3,10.3],[10.3,12.5],[12.5,13.1],[13.1,13.6],[13.6,14.2],[14.2,14.4],[14.4,15.4],[15.4,15.4],[15.4,15.9],[15.9,16.6],[16.6,17.4],[17.4,17.7],[17.7,18.58],[18.58,18.9],[19.76,20.26],[20.26,20.56],[20.56,20.76],[20.76,21.26],[21.26,22.36],[22.36,22.36],[22.36,23.36],[23.36,23.66],[23.66,24.86],[24.86,25.26],[25.26,25.76],[25.76,26.16],[26.16,27.46],[27.46,27.76],[27.76,27.86],[27.86,28.56],[28.84,29.66],[29.66,31.61],[31.61,31.86],[31.86,31.86],[31.86,31.86],[31.86,32.33],[32.56,32.71],[32.81,33.36],[33.36,34.36],[34.36,34.46],[34.46,34.96],[34.96,35.16],[35.16,36.46],[36.46,36.96],[36.96,37.46],[37.63,37.96],[38.64,39.34],[39.34,39.54],[39.54,40.14],[40.14,40.34],[40.34,41.34],[41.34,41.64],[41.64,41.74],[41.74,42.34],[42.34,42.64]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.3],[1.3,1.93],[2.0,2.4],[3.06,3.5],[3.5,3.9],[3.9,4.1],[4.1,4.5],[4.5,4.5],[4.5,6.4],[6.4,6.7],[6.7,6.97],[6.97,6.97],[6.97,7.0],[7.0,9.1],[9.1,9.5],[9.5,10.6],[10.6,10.8],[10.8,11.6],[11.6,12.3],[12.3,13.2],[13.2,13.7],[13.7,14.2],[14.2,14.59],[14.67,15.1],[15.1,16.1],[16.1,16.1],[16.1,16.6],[16.6,17.5],[17.5,18.3],[18.3,18.6],[18.6,19.5],[19.5,19.9],[20.6,21.2],[21.2,21.5],[21.5,21.7],[21.7,22.5],[22.5,23.5],[23.5,23.6],[23.6,24.6],[24.6,25.0],[25.0,26.29],[26.29,26.61],[26.61,26.61],[26.61,27.9],[27.9,29.4],[29.4,29.7],[29.7,29.8],[29.8,30.4],[30.4,31.8],[31.8,31.98],[31.98,32.02],[32.02,33.1],[33.1,34.2],[34.2,34.7],[34.8,35.16],[35.29,35.8